#+TITLE: org-llm — user-defined recipes (personal tier)
#+AUTHOR: you
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil
#+FILETAGS: :org-llm:recipes:personal:

# Copy this file to ~/org/org-llm-recipes.org to enable. The proxy
# auto-loads it (mtime-cached); no relaunch needed for new entries.
#
# Each :recipe:-tagged heading defines ONE personal recipe. Required
# properties: NAME, TARGET, PATTERN. The body (everything after :END:
# and before the next heading) is injected into the agent's prompt
# as advisory text when the pattern matches.
#
# Personal recipes WIN over shared recipes (the ones shipped in
# org_llm/orchestration.py) when both match the same input — your
# intent overrides the default.
#
# Patterns are compiled with re.IGNORECASE | re.DOTALL. Backslashes
# in patterns must be escaped per org-mode's text rules (\\b not \b).
#
# A malformed entry (missing required property, invalid regex) is
# silently skipped — a personal recipe must never crash the proxy.

* my_finance_summary                                              :recipe:
:PROPERTIES:
:NAME:    my_finance_summary
:TARGET:  researcher
:PATTERN: \b(net worth|balance|spending|budget|expenses?)\b
:END:

RECIPE — finance summary:
  1. Call the my_finance_query MCP tool with the user's window.
  2. Format the result with currency symbols and a 1-line trend
     comment.
  3. Cite the source ledger file in your reply.
Run STEP 1 → STEP 2 → STEP 3.

* my_reading_log                                                   :recipe:
:PROPERTIES:
:NAME:    my_reading_log
:TARGET:  researcher
:PATTERN: \b(what.{0,10}reading|finished reading|book.{0,5}log)\b
:END:

RECIPE — reading log lookup:
  1. Look in ~/org/reading-log.org for entries with =DONE= marks.
  2. Return the most recent 5 with title, author, finished date.
  3. If the user asked "currently reading", filter to in-progress
     items instead.

* override_count_for_my_workflow                                   :recipe:
:PROPERTIES:
:NAME:    my_count_override
:TARGET:  *
:PATTERN: how many times.*\b(commits?|prs?|merges?)\b
:END:

# This overrides the shared count_across_vault recipe ONLY when the
# user is asking about commits/PRs/merges — those route to my custom
# git-history tool instead of the org-mode regex search.

RECIPE — git activity count:
  1. Call my_git_query MCP tool with the time window from the question.
  2. Return the count and the top 3 commit messages.
